  "body": "## Summary\n\n* **What is the goal of this PR?** Prevent CSS parsing and cache loading from aborting or leaving an unusable cache when heap is constrained or input is malformed.\n* **What changes are included?**\n  * Replace the allocation-prone rules map with bounded flat storage for rule entries, selector text, and deduplicated styles. Every growth allocation is fallible.\n  * Replace CSS deduplication's throwing STL scratch containers with one optional nothrow table; allocation failure falls back to parsing every stylesheet.\n  * Return explicit complete, partial, and error outcomes. Oversized stylesheets and truncated selectors or declarations cannot be cached as complete.\n  * Validate cache headers, lengths, and serialized enum values before hydration.\n  * Write caches through a temporary file, preserve complete caches when a retry remains partial, and restore the previous backup if promotion fails.\n\n## Scope Check\n\nCrossPoint is intentionally narrow. See [SCOPE.md](../blob/master/SCOPE.md) and [ROADMAP.md](../blob/master/ROADMAP.md).\nPlease confirm:\n\n- [x] I have read SCOPE.md and ROADMAP.md.\n- [x] This PR is **not** a new built-in theme (themes are temporarily closed pending the move to SD-loaded themes).\n- [x] This PR is **not** a new external network connector (sync engine, cloud storage, remote file access, etc.).\n- [x] This PR is **not** an interactive app, writing tool, RSS/news/browser, media playback, or PDF feature.\n- [x] The stock firmware does not already handle this well, **and** no other popular CrossPoint fork already does without this backport.\n- [x] This PR does not touch `freeink-sdk/`, `lib/hal/`, the bootloader, OTA, or recovery code.\n\nNot applicable; this is reliability work in the existing EPUB CSS path.\n\n## Additional Context\n\nThis is the CSS follow-up separated from #2990 after its File Transfer fix merged. It began as an adaptation of Julia's [CrossInk fix](https://github.com/uxjulia/CrossInk/commit/9fb247545f1f9917a4246794f43b29ad9ff78238), then incorporated the explicit partial-cache and retry behavior discussed in #2990.\n\nThe bounded flat rule store follows the direction of #2602 while retaining this PR's cache-status, retry, validation, and rollback work. #3125 addresses only the old map-based cache loader and is therefore narrower than the current implementation here.\n\nRegression coverage includes:\n\n* continuing cascade updates for existing selectors after new-rule growth stops;\n* marking oversized selectors, declarations, and stylesheets partial;\n* complete and partial cache round trips;\n* rejection of corrupted serialized style values;\n* restoration of the only usable backup after a failed cache promotion.\n\nValidation passes 157/157 host tests, cppcheck, the repository formatting wrapper, `git diff --check`, and the ESP32-C3 default build. The final default image uses 54,540 bytes static RAM and 5,709,391 bytes flash. GitHub CI also passes all four firmware targets and CodeRabbit.\n\nNo allocation in the rule-store growth path can abort on OOM: failures return a partial result and keep already accepted rules usable for the current session.\n\n---\n\n### AI Usage\n\nWhile CrossPoint doesn't have restrictions on AI tools in contributing, please be transparent about their usage as it\nhelps set the right context for reviewers.\n\nDid you use AI tools to help write this code? **YES**\n\nAI tools were used to trace the earlier review findings, implement the backport, review failure paths, and run the test matrix.",
